     "result_text_tail": " come from the briefing pack or are calculated from it; there are no \"?\" placeholders. QA leaves one warning that doesn't matter: the pack writes the inventory holding as \"four months\" in words, so the checker can't match the figure 4.\n\n**Choices I made on your behalf**\n- **Audience:** the CEO and board deciding at the March 2027 meeting.\n- **Look:** the navy theme.\n- **Storyline:** I skipped the review checkpoint and built the storyline straight through.\n- **The $40M ambition:** I read it as $40M of US revenue by 2030 and tested every route against it.\n- **Option B's awareness band:** I placed Onsoo in the \"below 10%\" band using the 4% awareness among all skincare buyers. The 9% among K-beauty buyers gives the same band.\n- **Group margin:** one-time costs and fixtures count as expenses in the year they're paid; inventory counts as cash, not operating cost.\n- **Ignored figure:** the trade-press \"$5.2B US K-beauty market\" also counts makeup and hair care. It is footnoted as not comparable and not used.\n\n**Checks I couldn't run**\n- I couldn't look at the slides as images because no converter is installed here. Layout was checked only by the renderer's built-in overflow checks, so it's worth flipping through once in PowerPoint.\n- I didn't re-check sources online because there are no web sources.\n\nNext steps I can take: try another theme, or add per-SKU economics if you get them. The planning team applies the hero cream's unit economics to all seven SKUs, and the deck flags that."
